{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:389610478bbd6fba","name":"Security Specialist","source":{"id":"source:reference-389610478bbd6fba","title":"Security Specialist","revision":19760,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:33:42Z","sha256":"25c4353af73d513e02f6a2e6ab08b1d5fb7ba3464476f024326456072ad49017","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19760","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Security%20Specialist&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-389610478bbd6fba","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Every level of government has at least one law enforcement agency, and virtually all private organizations or individuals with sufficient resources have an independent security force on call. Starports and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Stations"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Stations","referenceId":"reference:65763f09c9074f45"},", due to their importance in interstellar commerce, always have a substantial security presence; similarly, all but the smallest private ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," have shipboard security to deter pirates, shipjackers, and mutineers.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Security Specialists act as bodyguards for VIPs and crisis response teams for cities and starports. Starports, in particular, are dangerous assignments due to the large crowds, constant movement, and intermingling ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", maximizing the chances of a terrible misunderstanding due to a language barrier or differences in local customs. Worse, starports might have to deal with a hostile ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," if a smuggler, pirate, or outlaw decides to blast his or her way off the planet. As a result, Security Specialists tend to be heavily armed (often using heavier ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", such as gunships) and paired with sharpshooters (as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Expert Assassins"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Expert_Assassins?action=edit&redlink=1"},").\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Security Specialist Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 5\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +9; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 16), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 21, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 16; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dodge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dodge","referenceId":"reference:9444f21689